structure DerivationData (m : MetricData V ι) (b : LieBracketData ℝ V) (A : Type uA) [CommRing A] [Algebra ℝ A] where
  D : V →ₗ[ℝ] A →ₗ[ℝ] A
  leibniz : ∀ (X : V) (f g : A), D X (f * g) = D X f * g + f * D X g
  bracket_deriv : ∀ (X Y : V) (f : A), D X (D Y f) - D Y (D X f) = D (b.bracket X Y) f

Then all lemmas take (dd : DerivationData m b A) and use dd.D, dd.leibniz, dd.bracket_deriv. The defs gamma/cG stay as-is (no D). The defs ui/H/etc. take (dd) (they use dd.D). This makes everything clean and the final theorem's hypotheses: {dd : DerivationData m b A} — a single expanded structure with the two axioms visible.

